; A stack group's saved accumulator holding a DTP-BODY-FORWARD is restored as
; saved and left alone by the scavenger (sys/ucadr/uc-stack-groups.lisp
; SG-LOAD-BLOCK-INTO-PDL-BUFFER, uc-storage-allocation.lisp SCAVL3).  Load
; lisp/sg-saved-body-forward.lisp first, interpreted or compiled.  Microcode
; that follows the forward from the leader slot halts in ILLOP on the page
; fault in no region (PC 24770 on microcode 2002), and the case gets no answer.
;
; Preconditions: the target address is in no region, the husk tenured, the
; stack group young.
(sgf-setup) => (T NIL T)
; The control: the stack group resumed with its saved M-A as it left it.
(funcall *sgf-sg*) => 1
; Resumed with a body-forward in its saved M-A (SG-LOAD-BLOCK-INTO-PDL-BUFFER).
(sgf-resume) => 1
; A young collection copies a young stack group whose saved M-A is a
; body-forward (SCAVL3 scavenges the copy's leader), which keeps the word and
; then resumes.
(sgf-collect) => (T T (DTP-BODY-FORWARD T) 1)
